WEBVTT

00:01:39.030 --> 00:01:42.450
Give it everything you've got, 
Wake Up, Girls!!

00:01:47.190 --> 00:01:48.440
Yoppi?

00:01:48.440 --> 00:01:49.720
I'm fine.

00:01:49.720 --> 00:01:51.960
We just have to do 
what we've been doing.

00:01:51.960 --> 00:01:53.800
Please get off the stage.

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.460
The I-1 Club's coming in.

00:02:06.450 --> 00:02:07.840
What am I going to do?

00:02:07.840 --> 00:02:09.880
What should I do?

00:02:09.880 --> 00:02:12.260
Why now?

00:02:12.260 --> 00:02:14.440
Why did this have to happen now?

00:02:15.340 --> 00:02:16.940
Yoppi, are you in there?

00:02:18.500 --> 00:02:19.300
Yeah.

00:02:19.300 --> 00:02:20.950
It's time to go.

00:02:20.950 --> 00:02:21.870
I'll be right there.

00:02:33.260 --> 00:02:34.880
What's wrong?

00:02:35.280 --> 00:02:37.720
Nothing. I was just 
pumping myself up.

00:02:37.720 --> 00:02:39.130
Really?

00:02:39.610 --> 00:02:41.900
Yoppi, we're rehearsing next.

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:42.640
Sorry.

00:02:43.260 --> 00:02:45.690
We only have ten minutes.

00:02:45.690 --> 00:02:46.670
Really?

00:02:48.390 --> 00:02:49.890
Huh? Aren't we going 
to form a circle?

00:02:51.090 --> 00:02:53.020
Keep it together, leader.

00:02:53.020 --> 00:02:54.150
Sorry.

00:02:56.190 --> 00:02:56.890
Here we go!

00:02:56.890 --> 00:02:57.760
We can do it!

00:02:57.760 --> 00:02:59.650
Wake Up, Girls!!

00:03:00.250 --> 00:03:01.910
We're going to start the music.

00:03:03.220 --> 00:03:05.830
Yoppi, you're standing 
in the wrong place.

00:03:05.830 --> 00:03:07.140
Sorry.

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:13.160
<i>Here we go</i>

00:03:13.160 --> 00:03:13.920
<i>We can do it</i>

00:03:13.920 --> 00:03:15.460
<i>Wake Up, Girls!</i>

00:03:15.460 --> 00:03:19.470
<i>Leave it up to us, everyone</i>

00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:26.220
<i>We'll eat up your problems, 
no matter how heavy</i>

00:03:21.390 --> 00:03:22.990
What's wrong with that center?

00:03:22.990 --> 00:03:24.590
She's off-tempo.

00:03:26.760 --> 00:03:28.220
Thank you!

00:03:28.220 --> 00:03:30.370
Thank you!

00:03:32.850 --> 00:03:34.900
Yoppi, is something wrong?

00:03:34.900 --> 00:03:35.560
What?

00:03:35.560 --> 00:03:37.840
Something's wrong with your leg.

00:03:37.840 --> 00:03:40.290
Did you hurt yourself 
when you tripped earlier?

00:03:42.040 --> 00:03:43.280
Huh? What?

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:44.990
What's going on?

00:03:48.260 --> 00:03:49.250
This is...

00:03:49.590 --> 00:03:51.860
I'm fine. It's not a problem.

00:03:51.860 --> 00:03:54.240
But it looks really painful.

00:03:54.240 --> 00:03:57.250
Yoppi, maybe you shouldn't strain yourself.

00:03:57.250 --> 00:03:59.530
It'll get worse.

00:04:00.510 --> 00:04:02.510
I just need to last five minutes.

00:04:02.510 --> 00:04:05.010
If I can handle that, I can still perform.

00:04:05.920 --> 00:04:06.760
That's impossible.

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:09.510
No! I refuse!

00:04:10.840 --> 00:04:11.880
Then...

00:04:11.880 --> 00:04:14.270
Then perform without me!

00:04:14.600 --> 00:04:15.350
What?

00:04:15.350 --> 00:04:17.840
Perform without me! Please!

00:04:17.840 --> 00:04:20.120
But without the center...

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:22.280
We can't train a substitute now.

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:23.960
President.

00:04:25.860 --> 00:04:27.610
I'm sorry.

00:04:27.610 --> 00:04:29.030
I'm sorry.

00:04:37.050 --> 00:04:38.040
Let's withdraw.

00:04:38.400 --> 00:04:39.420
What?

00:04:39.420 --> 00:04:41.300
You can't withdraw.

00:04:41.300 --> 00:04:42.050
You have to perform.

00:04:43.570 --> 00:04:45.400
Please, perform.

00:04:45.400 --> 00:04:47.430
No, let's withdraw.

00:04:49.120 --> 00:04:53.080
We may be able to perform without you.

00:04:53.080 --> 00:04:56.620
But a performance without 
you isn't good enough.

00:04:56.620 --> 00:04:57.430
What?

00:04:57.930 --> 00:05:00.690
After all, I can't accept it.

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:02.940
Mayushi.

00:05:02.940 --> 00:05:06.360
I think it's meaningless 
without you, too.

00:05:07.410 --> 00:05:10.710
The seven of us are Wake Up, Girls!.

00:05:10.710 --> 00:05:11.640
That's right.

00:05:11.640 --> 00:05:12.200
Yeah.

00:05:13.560 --> 00:05:14.710
But...

00:05:15.540 --> 00:05:18.960
I'm so sorry, everyone.

00:05:23.960 --> 00:05:27.220
Tohoku Block Representatives

00:05:25.010 --> 00:05:27.220
What should we do, President?

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:29.720
Well...

00:05:35.540 --> 00:05:37.980
Playing at friendship again?

00:05:38.980 --> 00:05:41.980
You haven't changed at all, Mayu.

00:05:43.330 --> 00:05:44.680
Were you eavesdropping?

00:05:44.680 --> 00:05:45.530
What poor taste.

00:05:46.130 --> 00:05:49.240
Shiho, sorry. Today we're...

00:05:49.240 --> 00:05:50.700
I won't let you quit.

00:05:53.380 --> 00:05:54.240
What?

00:06:00.520 --> 00:06:01.500
There.

00:06:04.470 --> 00:06:09.260
The bandages will only last 
you a few more hours today.

00:06:10.140 --> 00:06:13.040
Once your performance is over, 
make sure you go to the hospital.

00:06:13.040 --> 00:06:15.420
I will. Thank you.

00:06:18.640 --> 00:06:20.020
Shiho.

00:06:21.270 --> 00:06:22.020
Thanks.

00:06:24.320 --> 00:06:25.780
Whatever.

00:06:29.250 --> 00:06:31.220
She's actually pretty nice.

00:06:31.220 --> 00:06:34.130
Hold on. We shouldn't 
let our guard down.

00:06:34.130 --> 00:06:38.100
Yoppi, did they put thumbtacks 
under your bandages?

00:06:38.100 --> 00:06:40.420
If that were the case, 
she'd need surgery.

00:06:41.070 --> 00:06:42.340
Think you'll be okay?

00:06:42.340 --> 00:06:44.770
Yeah. I feel a lot better.

00:06:44.770 --> 00:06:45.800
That's great.

00:06:48.000 --> 00:06:51.050
Just to be sure, 
let's change our formation.

00:06:51.490 --> 00:06:52.680
Can you do it, girls?

00:06:53.740 --> 00:06:55.660
We should reduce any further risks.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:59.580
We should change 
the jump during the last hook.

00:06:59.580 --> 00:07:00.060
Yeah.

00:07:00.880 --> 00:07:01.830
I'm sorry.

00:07:01.830 --> 00:07:03.320
Leave it to us.

00:07:04.140 --> 00:07:06.520
Don't be so rough with it.

00:07:06.520 --> 00:07:08.930
It'd be bad luck if it broke.

00:07:08.930 --> 00:07:12.950
What? Didn't you say it'd be good 
if it broke like a good luck bracelet?

00:07:12.950 --> 00:07:14.950
It'd be more like the bad luck you get

00:07:14.950 --> 00:07:17.330
when the straps on your clogs break.

00:07:19.650 --> 00:07:21.080
Leader.

00:07:21.640 --> 00:07:24.080
Cheer up, leader.

00:07:27.940 --> 00:07:28.590
Okay.

00:07:32.700 --> 00:07:36.850
I'll do this instead of Yoppi here.

00:07:36.850 --> 00:07:41.100
Next, I'll come in and do this, right?

00:07:41.660 --> 00:07:42.350
Yeah.

00:07:44.870 --> 00:07:48.390
Make sure it looks like 
this is how it always was.

00:07:48.390 --> 00:07:49.190
Okay.

00:07:49.710 --> 00:07:51.390
How are you feeling, Yoppi?

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.110
Okay.

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:00.530
Are you okay?

00:08:00.530 --> 00:08:01.370
Yeah.

00:08:10.160 --> 00:08:14.380
The seven of them together 
make Wake Up, Girls!, huh?

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:20.640
That's right. No one can 
replace any of them.

00:08:21.380 --> 00:08:25.900
Wake Up, Girls! doesn't exist 
without all seven of them.

00:08:30.310 --> 00:08:31.100
Yes, ma'am.

00:08:38.180 --> 00:08:39.030
What do you think?

00:08:39.030 --> 00:08:42.290
We'll be okay. I think it's coming together.

00:08:42.290 --> 00:08:43.040
Yeah.

00:08:43.990 --> 00:08:46.040
Let's go, then.

00:08:46.040 --> 00:08:47.540
Yeah.

00:09:04.990 --> 00:09:07.420
The performance will 
begin in five minutes.

00:09:07.420 --> 00:09:11.070
Please return to your seats.

00:09:12.480 --> 00:09:13.700
Are you ready?

00:09:13.700 --> 00:09:14.760
Yes.

00:09:17.540 --> 00:09:18.820
It's starting.

00:09:30.040 --> 00:09:33.280
Thank you for coming.

00:09:33.280 --> 00:09:36.780
I am I-1's general manager, Shiraki.

00:09:39.360 --> 00:09:44.790
The finals of the Idol Festival are finally here.

00:09:44.790 --> 00:09:50.440
Today, in this I-1 Arena, 
in order to be officially recognized as

00:09:50.440 --> 00:09:53.580
I-1's rivals, the six groups 
from across the nation that made it

00:09:53.580 --> 00:09:55.860
through grueling preliminaries will compete.

00:09:56.630 --> 00:10:00.370
What is entertainment?

00:10:00.370 --> 00:10:02.120
What does it mean to be an idol?

00:10:03.130 --> 00:10:06.260
There is only one answer in my heart.

00:10:06.260 --> 00:10:09.850
The story begins on September 11, 2001,

00:10:09.850 --> 00:10:13.630
the day of the tragedy 
that occurred in New York.

00:10:14.470 --> 00:10:16.900
The opening of a new musical

00:10:16.900 --> 00:10:20.710
on Broadway had been 
planned for that day.

00:10:21.140 --> 00:10:23.930
However, immediately 
following the incident,

00:10:23.930 --> 00:10:26.440
a mood of self-restraint 
had spread throughout New York,

00:10:26.440 --> 00:10:29.650
and the opening was postponed.

00:10:30.330 --> 00:10:33.740
But in response to the hurt 
citizens of New York,

00:10:33.740 --> 00:10:36.170
the producer of the show felt now was

00:10:36.170 --> 00:10:43.600
the time for entertainment and 
raised the curtains as soon as possible.

00:10:43.600 --> 00:10:44.850
What is he talking about?

00:10:44.850 --> 00:10:45.960
9/11.

00:10:45.960 --> 00:10:47.000
Shhh...

00:10:47.490 --> 00:10:51.880
I believe this is the essence 
of entertainment,

00:10:51.880 --> 00:10:56.300
and I believe idols are a part of that.

00:10:57.830 --> 00:11:00.400
All the idols performing today

00:11:00.400 --> 00:11:03.860
are at the edges of this entertainment.

00:11:04.530 --> 00:11:08.910
Aiming for the top, 
they will compete here.

00:11:09.740 --> 00:11:15.770
Please show your support for all 
the idols appearing here today.

00:11:16.880 --> 00:11:21.530
The finals of the Idol Festival will now begin.

00:11:27.700 --> 00:11:29.890
The entire arena's full of I-1 fans!

00:11:29.890 --> 00:11:31.280
It's red everywhere you look!

00:11:31.280 --> 00:11:34.300
No one can beat our spirit and passion!

00:11:34.300 --> 00:11:37.560
It's time! Let's get this party started!

00:11:37.560 --> 00:11:39.090
Okay! Let's cheer!

00:11:39.090 --> 00:11:39.990
Here we go!

00:11:39.990 --> 00:11:40.880
You can do it!

00:11:40.880 --> 00:11:42.590
Wake Up, Girls!!

00:11:50.510 --> 00:11:52.560
We're the Akamiso All Stars!

00:11:52.920 --> 00:11:55.330
Thank you very much!

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:57.020
Can you go on, Yoshino?

00:11:57.720 --> 00:11:58.320
Yes.

00:11:59.510 --> 00:12:02.040
Are you okay, Yoppi?

00:12:02.040 --> 00:12:04.150
If it hurts, don't force yourself to perform.

00:12:04.150 --> 00:12:05.920
We'll cover you.

00:12:05.920 --> 00:12:07.290
Yoppi!

00:12:07.290 --> 00:12:09.240
Why are you crying now?

00:12:10.140 --> 00:12:11.170
Yoppi.

00:12:12.550 --> 00:12:14.810
It's been a year since then.

00:12:14.810 --> 00:12:15.510
What?

00:12:16.820 --> 00:12:18.960
Since our debut concert in Kotodai Park.

00:12:21.030 --> 00:12:25.440
I never imagined then 
that we'd be standing here now.

00:12:25.440 --> 00:12:28.870
But we really are here.

00:12:28.870 --> 00:12:29.810
Yeah.

00:12:30.390 --> 00:12:32.200
Let's give it our best.

00:12:32.200 --> 00:12:33.480
That's good enough for me.

00:12:33.480 --> 00:12:34.230
Yeah.

00:12:40.160 --> 00:12:40.980
Here we go!

00:12:40.980 --> 00:12:41.690
We can do it!

00:12:41.690 --> 00:12:44.610
Wake Up, Girls!!

00:12:44.610 --> 00:12:48.580
Good evening!

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:50.360
It's Shimada.

00:12:50.360 --> 00:12:51.580
Shimada Mayu, huh?

00:12:51.580 --> 00:12:53.800
I can't believe she's back.

00:12:53.800 --> 00:12:55.810
What does she think she's doing now?

00:12:56.650 --> 00:12:58.560
WUG's fired up!

00:12:58.560 --> 00:13:00.490
Let's show them what we can do!

00:13:00.490 --> 00:13:01.860
Yeah!

00:13:01.860 --> 00:13:06.900
Wake Up, Girls!! 
Wake Up, Girls!! Wake Up, Girls!!

00:13:12.630 --> 00:13:15.770
Good evening, everyone!

00:13:15.770 --> 00:13:17.180
We are...

00:13:17.180 --> 00:13:19.060
Wake Up, Girls!!

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.900
You can do it!

00:13:19.060 --> 00:13:21.900
WUG-chan!

00:13:23.730 --> 00:13:28.780
We're an idol unit based in Sendai.

00:13:28.780 --> 00:13:31.060
We're still not great at singing or dancing,

00:13:31.060 --> 00:13:33.290
but we'll do our best today.

00:13:33.290 --> 00:13:34.910
We hope you enjoy the show!

00:13:35.730 --> 00:13:39.130
This is "7 Girls War!"

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:40.990
You can do it!

00:13:40.990 --> 00:13:43.720
You can do it, WUG-chan!

00:13:47.350 --> 00:13:48.060
<i>Here we go</i>

00:13:48.060 --> 00:13:48.680
<i>We can do it</i>

00:13:48.680 --> 00:13:50.010
<i>Wake Up, Girls!</i>

00:13:50.010 --> 00:13:54.530
<i>Leave it up to us, everyone</i>

00:13:55.350 --> 00:14:00.690
<i>We'll eat up your problems, no matter how heavy 
(You eat too much) (What)</i>

00:14:00.690 --> 00:14:05.040
<i>Normally we don't 
have much confidence</i>

00:14:02.640 --> 00:14:04.470
Not bad.

00:14:05.040 --> 00:14:06.070
Matsuda.

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:08.690
Do you remember what 
I told you at the audition?

00:14:06.070 --> 00:14:13.260
<i>But we'll become anything to see you</i>

00:14:08.690 --> 00:14:10.700
What? No.

00:14:10.700 --> 00:14:13.260
About idols being a story.

00:14:13.260 --> 00:14:14.340
Oh.

00:14:14.340 --> 00:14:19.300
<i>We won't let you call us naïve</i>

00:14:14.720 --> 00:14:19.300
They've written tons 
of stories in this past year.

00:14:19.300 --> 00:14:22.010
<i>We're waking up</i>

00:14:19.590 --> 00:14:23.590
And today will become a new story.

00:14:22.010 --> 00:14:28.720
<i>In order to find happiness Take Off!</i>

00:14:24.540 --> 00:14:28.720
I know I shouldn't be saying this, 
but these girls are idols.

00:14:28.720 --> 00:14:30.240
<i>3, 2, 1, Go!</i>

00:14:30.240 --> 00:14:35.270
<i>Largely largely Changing (Changing)</i>

00:14:35.670 --> 00:14:40.270
<i>It's not easy</i>

00:14:40.270 --> 00:14:45.650
<i>But you're by our side</i>

00:14:45.650 --> 00:14:51.320
<i>We find the courage to take a step 
(All right, let's go)</i>

00:14:51.320 --> 00:14:56.660
<i>Our dreams are still far away 
(So Far)</i>

00:14:57.050 --> 00:15:01.700
<i>It's not that we're in a hurry</i>

00:15:00.050 --> 00:15:00.930
Hey.

00:15:00.930 --> 00:15:02.070
They're surprisingly good.

00:15:01.700 --> 00:15:06.670
<i>With even stronger feelings</i>

00:15:02.070 --> 00:15:02.930
Yeah.

00:15:07.030 --> 00:15:13.320
<i>Tomorrow we'll surely 
be Shining Star</i>

00:15:08.680 --> 00:15:09.960
Yeah!

00:15:20.850 --> 00:15:42.120
WUG! WUG! WUG! WUG!

00:15:28.190 --> 00:15:31.360
WUG! WUG! WUG! WUG!

00:15:42.120 --> 00:15:46.800
<i>At times we must bear disappointment</i>

00:15:46.800 --> 00:15:52.130
<i>At times we shed tears</i>

00:15:52.130 --> 00:15:57.760
<i>But the tears we shed together</i>

00:15:57.760 --> 00:16:02.750
<i>Become seven stars</i>

00:16:02.310 --> 00:16:02.960
Mayu, I'm jumping.

00:16:02.750 --> 00:16:07.400
<i>Shine shine</i>

00:16:02.960 --> 00:16:03.400
What?

00:16:07.400 --> 00:16:09.030
<i>3, 2, 1, Go!</i>

00:16:09.030 --> 00:16:14.420
<i>We are reborn Changing 
(Changing)</i>

00:16:14.420 --> 00:16:18.910
<i>It's not easy</i>

00:16:18.910 --> 00:16:24.210
<i>But you're by our side</i>

00:16:24.210 --> 00:16:29.920
<i>We find the courage to take a step 
(All right, let's go)</i>

00:16:29.920 --> 00:16:35.880
<i>Our dreams are still far away 
(So Far)</i>

00:16:35.880 --> 00:16:40.270
<i>It's not that we're in a hurry</i>

00:16:40.270 --> 00:16:45.600
<i>With even stronger feelings</i>

00:16:45.600 --> 00:16:51.800
<i>Tomorrow we'll surely 
be Shining Star</i>

00:16:53.610 --> 00:16:54.780
The audience is fired up.

00:16:54.780 --> 00:16:56.280
This is amazing.

00:16:56.280 --> 00:16:57.970
You were right, Shihocchi.

00:16:57.970 --> 00:17:00.070
It must be because 
Hayasaka's song is so good.

00:17:00.070 --> 00:17:00.940
It's not that.

00:17:00.940 --> 00:17:02.150
The song has nothing to do with it.

00:17:02.150 --> 00:17:04.750
The hard work of the members 
is coming through.

00:17:04.750 --> 00:17:06.370
Let's get ready.

00:17:06.370 --> 00:17:08.650
We'd better do our best, too.

00:17:08.650 --> 00:17:09.130
Yeah.

00:17:09.730 --> 00:17:11.380
I won't lose.

00:17:12.870 --> 00:17:14.240
Harder than anyone!

00:17:14.240 --> 00:17:15.490
More beautiful than anyone!

00:17:15.490 --> 00:17:16.760
More precise than anyone!

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.760
I-1 Club, let's go!

00:17:18.760 --> 00:17:19.760
Yeah!

00:17:27.310 --> 00:17:31.350
You're the best, WUG-chan!

00:17:34.700 --> 00:17:36.540
Thank you very much!

00:17:36.540 --> 00:17:38.700
Thank you very much!

00:17:39.640 --> 00:18:04.560
Wake Up, Girls!! 
Wake Up, Girls!! Wake Up, Girls!!

00:18:05.120 --> 00:18:07.370
Your scores, please.

00:18:07.370 --> 00:18:08.730
Who should we choose?

00:18:08.730 --> 00:18:11.310
It's a difficult choice.

00:18:11.650 --> 00:18:13.360
Shiraki-san.

00:18:14.050 --> 00:18:17.970
I wonder if the guerrilla 
concerts you used to put on

00:18:17.970 --> 00:18:20.210
at Azuma Bridge smelled like this.

00:18:20.210 --> 00:18:21.830
Not that I ever saw one.

00:18:36.130 --> 00:18:38.870
Thank you for waiting, everyone!

00:18:38.870 --> 00:18:41.390
Before the results, we have 
a special guest appearance!

00:18:41.390 --> 00:18:43.750
I-1 Club!

00:18:51.370 --> 00:18:52.860
Yoshino, are you okay?

00:18:52.860 --> 00:18:54.070
Yes.

00:19:05.410 --> 00:19:06.760
Good job.

00:19:13.660 --> 00:19:15.630
Good evening, everyone!

00:19:15.940 --> 00:19:18.460
We're the I-1 Club!

00:19:19.700 --> 00:19:23.890
Are you enjoying the 2014 Idol Festival?

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:32.400
<i>I believe there are three ways 
to make people happy.</i>

00:19:34.080 --> 00:19:37.400
<i>There are those who make many 
people happy throughout the world.</i>

00:19:37.960 --> 00:19:41.150
This is "First-Rate Smile!"

00:19:42.640 --> 00:19:46.910
<i>Those who make those 
around themselves happy.</i>

00:19:50.680 --> 00:19:54.170
That's where you used 
to be standing, Mayushi.

00:19:55.480 --> 00:19:59.420
No. I belong with Wake Up, Girls!.

00:20:00.290 --> 00:20:01.420
Yeah.

00:20:03.300 --> 00:20:06.680
<i>And those who make themselves happy.</i>

00:20:07.430 --> 00:20:09.890
It's time to announce the results.

00:20:09.890 --> 00:20:14.690
The winner of the 2014 
Idol Festival is...

00:20:17.090 --> 00:20:20.320
From Chubu, the Akamiso All Stars!

00:20:23.570 --> 00:20:25.370
They won.

00:20:27.580 --> 00:20:30.510
Let's have another 
round of applause for all

00:20:30.510 --> 00:20:32.830
the idols who participated today!

00:20:34.020 --> 00:20:37.840
<i>There's one other thing 
I learned about happiness.</i>

00:20:38.690 --> 00:20:44.090
<i>It's that you can't make anyone 
happy if you're not happy yourself.</i>

00:20:46.070 --> 00:20:52.400
<i>That's why I think I might be 
able to make someone happy now.</i>

00:20:53.120 --> 00:20:54.600
Green Leaves Entertainment

00:20:56.870 --> 00:20:58.610
Shouldn't you answer the phone?

00:20:58.920 --> 00:21:00.790
You answer it.

00:21:00.790 --> 00:21:02.610
If it's the real estate agency, 
tell them I'm not here.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:06.280
It's your fault for rashly signing a contract.

00:21:02.610 --> 00:21:13.370
<b>Go get some work!!</b>

00:21:06.280 --> 00:21:09.890
Just tell them you can't sign it 
because the situation has changed.

00:21:09.890 --> 00:21:11.610
No way. That's too much work.

00:21:11.610 --> 00:21:13.370
There she goes again.

00:21:13.840 --> 00:21:16.540
I paid the deposit. 
I'm too injured to go on.

00:21:16.540 --> 00:21:18.760
Draw, even, safe.

00:21:18.760 --> 00:21:19.380
What?

00:21:19.780 --> 00:21:21.170
You're unbelievable.

00:21:21.170 --> 00:21:23.230
This is Green Leaves.

00:21:24.100 --> 00:21:25.380
What? Yes.

00:21:26.280 --> 00:21:28.790
Um... One moment, please.

00:21:28.790 --> 00:21:30.880
I'll connect you to our president, Tange.

00:21:30.880 --> 00:21:33.000
I told you to tell them I'm not here!

00:21:33.000 --> 00:21:34.020
They can hear you.

00:21:34.020 --> 00:21:35.100
Oh, well.

00:21:35.100 --> 00:21:36.300
It's not them.

00:21:36.300 --> 00:21:38.770
It's from a Tokyo record 
company named Bivex.

00:21:39.150 --> 00:21:41.800
Bivex? They're a major label.

00:21:41.800 --> 00:21:43.010
Why are they calling us?

00:21:43.010 --> 00:21:43.780
Who knows?

00:21:46.720 --> 00:21:49.280
Yes, I'm Tange, the president.

00:21:51.200 --> 00:21:52.540
A mainstream debut?

00:21:53.140 --> 00:21:55.910
Bivex wants to sign Wake Up, Girls!!

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:56.910
What? You're kidding!

00:21:57.280 --> 00:21:58.370
You're lying!

00:21:58.640 --> 00:22:00.400
I wouldn't lie about this!

00:22:00.400 --> 00:22:03.770
They liked you after 
seeing you at the Idol Festival!

00:22:03.770 --> 00:22:05.950
We're going to take it 
to the top this time!

00:22:05.950 --> 00:22:07.130
What?

00:22:07.500 --> 00:22:09.890
Green Leaves and Wake Up, Girls! are...

00:22:09.890 --> 00:22:11.890
What's going to happen?

00:22:11.890 --> 00:22:14.890
The End
